   "source": [
    "# Mice Protein Expression — Classification Model\n",
    "### Steps 5-7: Train/Test Split, Random Forest Classifier, Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook picks up directly from the EDA notebook (`mice_protein_eda.ipynb`). We classify each mouse into one of the **8 experimental groups** using its 77 protein expression levels.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Approach:** to avoid data leakage, the data is split into train/test *first*, and the KNN imputer is fit only on the training data before being applied unchanged to the test set — the model never gets to \"see\" test-set values while filling in missing ones. On top of that, this notebook adds cross-validation, permutation importance, and a significance check on the EDA/model overlap.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "60b5deed",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Train/Test Split + Label Encoding + Imputation (Leakage-Safe)\n",
    "\n",
    "**The correct order of operations is:**\n",
    "1. Split raw (still-missing) data into train/test first.\n",
    "2. Fit `KNNImputer` on the training set ONLY.\n",
    "3. Use that *same fitted imputer* to transform the test set (`.transform`, not `.fit_transform`).\n",
    "\n",
    "This guarantees the test set's values are filled in using only patterns learned from training data — no information from test mice leaks into how we impute training mice, or vice versa.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "09b7c8e6",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-17T05:52:53.327319Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-07-17T05:52:53.327150Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-07-17T05:52:54.996915Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-07-17T05:52:54.994716Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import KNNImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, StratifiedKFold, cross_val_score, GridSearchCV\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.inspection import permutation_importance\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix, classification_report, accuracy_score\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_style(\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.dpi\"] = 100\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "\n",
    "RANDOM_STATE = 42\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "aac77c32",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-07-17T05:52:54.999821Z",
