   "source": [
    "**Interpretation:** The stratified split kept class proportions nearly identical between train and test — every class matches to within 0.1 percentage point (e.g. `c-CS-m` is 13.9% of both train and test, `t-CS-s` is 9.7% of both). This confirms `stratify=y` did its job, so any accuracy difference between train and test can't be blamed on the split accidentally over- or under-representing a group.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why 80/20?** With only 1080 mice total, an 80/20 split still leaves ~216 mice for testing — enough for a stable per-class accuracy estimate while keeping most data for training.\n"
   ]
